======== question 2.1: Valley3BeforeNine on a running arm ========
  a running arm is an arm of a basepoint at L+5 that reaches L+9 with
  nothing at L+2 or below before its first such time (HighRunG/HighRunT).
  Valley3BeforeNine is read by its own definition: a peak at L+6 or above
  at arm index three or more, a time at L+3 or below five steps later, and
  every ascent to L+9 at least six steps after that.

